{
 "comment": [
  "When a GPU counts as throttled (health/rules.rs throttle_verdict, rule gpu-throttle). The node agent and the UI's throttleVerdict read the same file.",
  "HW slowdown, HW thermal slowdown and HW power brake slowdown always count. SW power cap, SW thermal slowdown and sync boost (and any reason not listed) count only while the GPU is busy:",
  "utilPct >= busyUtilPct and smClockMhz < clockBelow x clockMaxMhz (clock check skipped when clockMaxMhz is unknown), or powerW >= powerAt x powerLimitW when a limit is reported.",
  "GPU idle, Applications clocks setting and Display clock setting never count. An unreadable GPU (readable false) has no verdict.",
  "verdicts: one reading -> throttled and the message. cases: a reading every second from t=0, segment after segment, each segment cycling its readings;",
  "the alert is raised at raisedAtS (the condition must hold forS) and resolved at resolvedAtS (gone for clearS), or never (null).",
  "The idle alternation is real: all four GB10s at P8, 4 W, 208 of 3003 MHz reported [] and [\"SW power cap\"] on alternate readings (Live tour, Oct 29).",
  "November 7 cell1 Qwen3-0.6B capture: 96% utilization at 2444 of 3003 MHz, with no clock-event reason. A lower clock alone is not throttling. No busy SW-power-cap observation was captured; its existing warning policy stays unchanged."
 ],
 "rule": {
  "forS": 60,
  "clearS": 120,
  "busyUtilPct": 50,
  "clockBelow": 0.9,
  "powerAt": 0.8,
  "always": [
   "HW slowdown",
   "HW thermal slowdown",
   "HW power brake slowdown"
  ],
  "whenBusy": [
   "SW power cap",
   "SW thermal slowdown",
   "Sync boost"
  ],
  "never": [
   "GPU idle",
   "Applications clocks setting",
   "Display clock setting"
  ]
 },
